  "natural_discovery_routes": [
    "Route A (product name -> price): POST /v1/products/search q='name:\\'FIRSTCALL Test Plan\\'' (S34) -> product id -> GET /v1/prices?product=prod_... (S20 documented `product` filter) -> Price id.",
    "Route B (search prices): POST /v1/prices/search (S35) constrained by product/metadata -> Price id.",
    "Route C (enumerate): GET /v1/prices (S20); a disposable test account holds few prices, so the intended active price is directly enumerable.",
    "Route D (stable key): GET /v1/prices?lookup_keys[]=... (S20) if the fixture price carries a lookup_key (S28/S33) -- Stripe's documented deployment-stable reference.",
    "Route E (agent-native/live): Stripe Agent skills + plugins configure the Stripe MCP server exposing live account data, plus `stripe agent setup` and terminal `stripe docs` (S43) -- direct machine enumeration of the account's real Prices.",
    "Note: the customer task supplies the exact product name and explicitly permits read-only API exploration, so routes A-E are all inside the permitted, unmodified official surface."
  ],
